Module database for the Module picker (admin task)
==================================================

The Generic environment no longer has a configure step. The Module picker
reads its databases from the shared location set as "module_db_root" in
schemas/create.schema.json (and in the shared component
$DRONA_RUNTIME_DIR/form_components/drona_module_picker.json):

  /var/www/ood/apps/sys/dor-hprc-drona-composer-prod/environments/Generic/modules

The file for a toolchain is <module_db_root>/<toolchain value>.sqlite3,
e.g. modules.sqlite3 for "No toolchain (default)".

An admin builds or refreshes these files by hand with generate_modules_db.py,
in a scratch directory, then copies them into place:

  # default (no toolchain)
  ./generate_modules_db.py -b            # writes modules.sqlite3 here

  # a toolchain, e.g. foss/2025a
  ./generate_modules_db.py -b -t foss/2025a

The script names a toolchain file modules-foss_2025a.sqlite3, but the picker
looks for <module_db_root>/<toolchain value>.sqlite3, i.e. with value
"modules-foss/2025a" the path modules-foss/2025a.sqlite3. Copy it into place
under that name:

  mkdir -p <module_db_root>/modules-foss
  cp modules-foss_2025a.sqlite3 <module_db_root>/modules-foss/2025a.sqlite3

To offer a new toolchain, add it under "toolchains" in
$DRONA_RUNTIME_DIR/form_components/drona_module_picker.json:

      { "label": "foss/2025a", "value": "modules-foss/2025a" }
